---
// How booking works. Fourth of the four "Meet the team" pages
// (src/data/meetTheTeam.ts), and the one the brand foundation asks for
// explicitly: §3.5 names "a simple three-step how booking works section"
// as a category convention, with the three steps as check your area, choose
// your service, pick a date, because it "reduces friction for clients moving
// from a text-message habit to online booking".
//
// This page is that section, expanded into its own page. The homepage keeps
// the short version ("Easy to book, local to the core", index.astro v6,
// client copy, verbatim); this page is where the detail goes so the homepage
// does not have to carry it. The two are written not to repeat each other,
// per the brand foundation's "cover each point once".
//
// SOURCES. Everything factual here comes from index.astro's v6 copy and FAQ,
// which is client-supplied and therefore approved: booking by online, text,
// phone or email; a reminder in the lead-up and a message on the way; not
// needing to be home; how we get in being agreed at booking; quoting on the
// actual place; no lock-in, no minimum term, no exit fee; first clean taking
// longer. Nothing on this page is invented past that.
//
// BLOCKS LAUNCH:
//  1. PAYMENT IS NOT ANSWERED ANYWHERE ON THIS PAGE, and this is the page a
//     reader looks for it on. There is nothing in the repo about invoicing,
//     card payment, timing, deposits or cancellation fees. It is HELD BACK
//     rather than guessed: a wrong answer about money on the booking page is
//     the most expensive kind of placeholder. Add a "How do I pay?" FAQ and
//     a cancellation-window answer as soon as both are confirmed. Note that
//     why-tlb.astro's own FAQ tells readers most cleaning businesses publish
//     a 24 to 48 hour cancellation window, so a reader arrives here already
//     expecting TLB to state its own.
//  2. THE TWO BOOKING URLS DO NOT EXIST. /book/ and /quote/ are the
//     guessed slugs navigation.ts has carried sitewide since it was written.
//     Every page links them, but this is the page whose entire subject is
//     that flow, so it is the page where the 404 is least survivable.
//  3. "Book online in a couple of minutes" is index.astro's own client copy
//     and this page repeats the promise in its H1. Confirm the booking flow
//     genuinely takes a couple of minutes before launch, because the page
//     sets that expectation twice.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/sections/SiteHeader.astro';
import Hero from '../components/sections/Hero.astro';
import TrustBar from '../components/sections/TrustBar.astro';
import Backdrop from '../components/ui/Backdrop.astro';
import TextBlock from '../components/sections/TextBlock.astro';
import PhotoGallery from '../components/sections/PhotoGallery.astro';
import ContentGrid from '../components/sections/ContentGrid.astro';
import Callout from '../components/sections/Callout.astro';
import ServiceBlocks from '../components/sections/ServiceBlocks.astro';
import TagCloud from '../components/sections/TagCloud.astro';
import Faq from '../components/sections/Faq.astro';
import CallToAction from '../components/sections/CallToAction.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/sections/SiteFooter.astro';
import logoImg from '../assets/logo/tlb-logo-horizontal.png';
import footerLogoImg from '../assets/logo/tlb-logo-square.png';
import {
  primaryNav,
  headerNav,
  headerSecondaryCta,
  footerServiceLinks,
  footerContact,
  footerCopyright,
  quoteCta,
} from '../data/navigation';
import { locationGroups } from '../data/locations';
import { trustBarCards } from '../data/trust';
import { meetTheTeamBusiness, otherMeetTheTeamPages } from '../data/meetTheTeam';
import { z } from 'astro/zod';
import { getPage } from '../lib/cms';
import * as section from '../lib/cms-schemas';

// CONTENT lives in src/content/pages/how-booking-works.yaml and is edited in
// Pages CMS ("How booking works"). This file owns the layout: which sections
// appear, in what order, and how they look. The notes below explain why each
// section says what it says, and they stay here because Pages CMS rewrites the
// YAML file on save and would drop them.
//
// hero: the moment the booking turns into a person at your door, generated
// for this page. Booking itself is a screen, and IMAGE-GUIDELINES §4 bans
// lettering in frame, so a photograph of the flow is not possible: the
// honest subject is what the flow produces.
//
// definition: shares the hero photo behind a Cream scrim with the trust bar.
// Answer-target sentences per the brand foundation §3.6.2: "how do I book a
// cleaner in the Northern Rivers" is the query this page exists to answer,
// and the answer should survive being lifted out of the page.
//
// steps: PhotoGallery's `story` variant. That variant exists for exactly
// this: a sequence with a step label, a connector drawn between consecutive
// steps, and sides that alternate by array order. Deliberately NOT
// PathwayCards, which numbers cards to route different audiences to different
// destinations. These three are one route in order, and the numbering means
// sequence rather than choice. The steps are the brand foundation §3.5's own
// three, with its wording kept as the intent and the copy written to this
// site's voice. All three photos are REUSED, per IMAGE-GUIDELINES §5's "reuse
// before generating": each already means, elsewhere on this site, exactly
// what its step needs it to mean here:
//   1. a home in the hinterland, from the locations set
//   2. a homeowner and a cleaner talking, from the appliances set
//   3. a living room kept up by regular visits, from the deep cleaning set
//
// onTheDay: dark, because it is the pivot: everything above is the
// arrangement, everything below is the practical detail.
//
// practical: the four practical answers, two columns. Written as the
// questions a client asks in the first week rather than as features.
// ⚠️ A FIFTH CELL IS MISSING AND IT IS THE ONE ABOUT MONEY. See blocker 1 at
// the top of this file. Do not add it until payment terms and a cancellation
// window are confirmed.
//
// notOnline: the callout that makes the page's real point. Every competitor's
// booking page is an argument for their app; the brand foundation §1.5.5 is
// explicit that TLB's position is big-brand convenience without giving up the
// person, which means the online flow has to be offered rather than insisted on.
//
// otherBookings: three rows, each to the page that covers it, because the
// flow genuinely differs for these three and a host or an agency reading the
// three steps above will wonder if it applies to them.
//
// faq: every answer is index.astro's v6 client copy, restated for this page's
// context rather than repeated verbatim, or a direct consequence of it.
// ⚠️ TWO QUESTIONS ARE HELD BACK, both about money, and both belong here:
// "How do I pay?" and "What happens if I cancel late?" See blocker 1.
const page = await getPage(
  'how-booking-works',
  z.object({
    seo: section.seo,
    // The hero photo also sits behind the trust bar (see the Backdrop below),
    // so it cannot be left empty.
    hero: section.hero.extend({ image: section.requiredImage }),
    definition: section.textBlock,
    steps: section.storySteps,
    onTheDay: section.textBlock,
    practical: section.textGrid,
    notOnline: section.callout,
    otherBookings: section.linkList,
    whereWeClean: section.tagCloud,
    faq: section.faq,
    beforeYouBook: section.sectionIntro,
    closingCta: section.callToAction,
  }),
);

const pageMeta = {
  ...page.seo,
  canonical: 'https://tlbcleaning.com.au/how-booking-works/',
};

const business = meetTheTeamBusiness(pageMeta.description);

// This page leads with "Book your clean online" rather than the sitewide
// "Get an instant quote", because it is the one page whose subject is the
// booking flow itself. It is the same headerSecondaryCta every page's header
// already carries, so it is not a new label to maintain, and the brand
// foundation §2.4 names it the primary website CTA.
const bookCta = headerSecondaryCta;

const heroImage = { ...page.hero.image, ratio: '4/3' };

const bookingSteps = page.steps.steps.map((step) => ({
  ...step,
  image: { ...step.image, ratio: '4/3' },
}));

const practicalBlocks = page.practical.items.map((item) => ({
  type: 'text' as const,
  ...item,
  tone: 'muted' as const,
}));

// Cross-links to the other three pages in this cluster.
const clusterItems = otherMeetTheTeamPages('/how-booking-works/');
---

<Base title={pageMeta.title} description={pageMeta.description} canonical={pageMeta.canonical} business={business}>
  <SiteHeader
    logo={{ label: 'TLB Cleaning', src: logoImg }}
    primaryNav={primaryNav}
    serviceNav={headerNav}
    secondaryCta={headerSecondaryCta}
    cta={quoteCta}
  />

  <main id="main">
    <Hero
      variant="split-single-image"
      imagePosition="right"
      kicker={page.hero.kicker}
      headingLines={page.hero.headingLines}
      lead={page.hero.lead}
      cta={bookCta}
      image={heroImage}
    />

    {/* Trust bar and definition block share ONE photo behind the Cream scrim, laid
        out across both. 90%, raised from 75% on 29 Sep 2026. Measured over
        this frame's own darkest region under the copy column, 75% gave 4.12:1
        — an AA FAIL. 90% gives 5.91:1. Backdrop.astro's `opacity` doc carries
        the method. It follows the hero photo, so re-check the contrast if an
        editor swaps that photo in Pages CMS. */}
    <Backdrop image={heroImage.src} tint="muted" opacity={90} focus="center">
      <TrustBar variant="card" cards={trustBarCards} />
      <TextBlock theme="muted" align="left" heading={page.definition.heading} body={page.definition.body} />
    </Backdrop>

    <PhotoGallery variant="story" heading={page.steps.heading} lead={page.steps.lead} steps={bookingSteps} />

    <TextBlock theme="dark" align="left" heading={page.onTheDay.heading} body={page.onTheDay.body} />

    <ContentGrid heading={page.practical.heading} lead={page.practical.lead} columns={2} blocks={practicalBlocks} />

    <Callout tone="note" heading={page.notOnline.heading} body={page.notOnline.body} />

    <ServiceBlocks
      variant="list"
      heading={page.otherBookings.heading}
      lead={page.otherBookings.lead}
      items={page.otherBookings.items}
    />

    <TagCloud
      heading={page.whereWeClean.heading}
      subheading={page.whereWeClean.subheading}
      groups={locationGroups}
      note={page.whereWeClean.note}
    />

    <Faq heading={page.faq.heading} items={page.faq.items} />

    <ServiceBlocks
      variant="list"
      heading={page.beforeYouBook.heading}
      lead={page.beforeYouBook.lead}
      items={clusterItems}
    />

    <CallToAction
      variant="secondary"
      kicker={page.closingCta.kicker}
      heading={page.closingCta.heading}
      lead={page.closingCta.lead}
      cta={bookCta}
    />
  </main>

  <SiteFooter
    logo={{ label: 'TLB Cleaning', src: footerLogoImg }}
    columns={[
      { title: 'Services', links: footerServiceLinks },
      { title: 'Locations', links: [{ label: 'View all locations', href: '/locations/' }] },
    ]}
    contact={footerContact}
    copyright={footerCopyright}
  />
</Base>
